WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:01.395
At the Airport.

2
00:00:01.675 --> 00:00:05.985
Day 28 of the Soft Skill Playbook course, in the Everyday Life phase.

3
00:00:07.735 --> 00:00:08.759
The key idea.

4
00:00:09.039 --> 00:00:13.092
An airport is a series of short conversations with people who are busy.

5
00:00:13.372 --> 00:00:18.897
Have your documents ready, answer exactly what's asked, and don't be shy about asking for help.

6
00:00:20.247 --> 00:00:21.101
Part 1.

7
00:00:21.381 --> 00:00:22.618
Your airport journey.

8
00:00:23.868 --> 00:00:24.785
Step 1:

9
00:00:25.065 --> 00:00:26.473
Check-in and bag drop.

10
00:00:26.753 --> 00:00:27.671
Step 2:

11
00:00:27.951 --> 00:00:29.167
Security screening.

12
00:00:29.447 --> 00:00:30.364
Step 3:

13
00:00:30.644 --> 00:00:33.524
Immigration or passport control: international.

14
00:00:33.804 --> 00:00:34.764
Step 4:

15
00:00:35.044 --> 00:00:36.217
Gate and boarding.

16
00:00:36.497 --> 00:00:37.457
Step 5:

17
00:00:37.737 --> 00:00:38.655
On the plane.

18
00:00:38.935 --> 00:00:39.873
Step 6:

19
00:00:40.153 --> 00:00:42.799
Arrival: immigration, baggage, customs.

20
00:00:44.149 --> 00:00:45.002
Part 1.

21
00:00:45.282 --> 00:00:46.434
Check-in counter.

22
00:00:47.684 --> 00:00:48.793
What you'll be asked.

23
00:00:49.073 --> 00:00:50.417
Here is a quick table:

24
00:00:50.697 --> 00:00:52.233
They ask, and You answer.

25
00:00:52.513 --> 00:00:55.372
May I see your passport or ID and ticket, please?:

26
00:00:55.652 --> 00:00:56.804
Sure, here you go.

27
00:00:57.084 --> 00:00:58.620
Where are you flying to today?:

28
00:00:58.900 --> 00:01:01.311
To Singapore, then connecting to Sydney.

29
00:01:01.591 --> 00:01:03.340
How many bags are you checking in?:

30
00:01:03.620 --> 00:01:05.519
Just one, and one cabin bag.

31
00:01:05.799 --> 00:01:07.420
Did you pack your bags yourself?:

32
00:01:07.700 --> 00:01:08.767
Yes, I did.

33
00:01:09.047 --> 00:01:13.036
Are you carrying any batteries, power banks, or liquids in your checked bag?:

34
00:01:13.316 --> 00:01:15.641
No, the power bank is in my cabin bag.

35
00:01:15.921 --> 00:01:17.095
Window or aisle?:

36
00:01:17.375 --> 00:01:18.441
Aisle, please.

37
00:01:18.721 --> 00:01:20.577
Your bag is 3 kg over.

38
00:01:20.857 --> 00:01:22.287
There's an excess charge.:

39
00:01:22.567 --> 00:01:25.340
Could I move some items to my cabin bag instead?

40
00:01:26.690 --> 00:01:27.799
What you can ask.

41
00:01:28.079 --> 00:01:30.383
Could I get an aisle or window seat, please?

42
00:01:30.663 --> 00:01:33.245
Is it possible to sit together with my colleague?

43
00:01:33.525 --> 00:01:38.325
Is my bag checked through to my final destination, or do I collect it in transit?

44
00:01:38.605 --> 00:01:41.015
What time does boarding start, and which gate?

45
00:01:41.295 --> 00:01:44.751
Is there any extra legroom or exit row seat available?

46
00:01:45.031 --> 00:01:47.165
What's the baggage allowance on this ticket?

47
00:01:47.445 --> 00:01:49.471
Can I add my frequent flyer number?

48
00:01:50.821 --> 00:01:52.187
Is the flight on time?

49
00:01:53.537 --> 00:01:54.411
Part 2.

50
00:01:54.691 --> 00:01:55.630
Security.

51
00:01:56.880 --> 00:01:58.224
Here is a quick table:

52
00:01:58.504 --> 00:02:00.531
You'll hear, and Meaning or what to do.

53
00:02:00.811 --> 00:02:02.752
Laptops and liquids out, please.:

54
00:02:03.032 --> 00:02:08.323
Put laptop and liquids ( at most 100 ml, in a clear bag) in a separate tray.

55
00:02:08.603 --> 00:02:09.989
Anything in your pockets?:

56
00:02:10.269 --> 00:02:12.787
Wallet, phone, keys, coins go in the tray.

57
00:02:13.067 --> 00:02:15.563
Please remove your belt or shoes or jacket.:

58
00:02:15.843 --> 00:02:17.208
Do it, place in tray.

59
00:02:17.488 --> 00:02:18.683
Step through, please.

60
00:02:18.963 --> 00:02:19.837
Arms up.:

61
00:02:20.117 --> 00:02:22.123
Walk through the scanner or body scanner.

62
00:02:22.403 --> 00:02:23.469
Is this your bag?

63
00:02:23.749 --> 00:02:24.923
I need to check it.:

64
00:02:25.203 --> 00:02:26.440
Yes, sure, go ahead.

65
00:02:26.720 --> 00:02:27.680
Stay calm.

66
00:02:27.960 --> 00:02:29.432
Random checks are normal.

67
00:02:30.782 --> 00:02:31.763
You can ask:

68
00:02:32.043 --> 00:02:34.774
Do I need to take out my tablet or charger too?

69
00:02:35.054 --> 00:02:36.505
Can I keep my shoes on?

70
00:02:37.855 --> 00:02:38.751
Part 3.

71
00:02:39.031 --> 00:02:40.737
Immigration (international).

72
00:02:41.987 --> 00:02:42.755
Info:

73
00:02:43.035 --> 00:02:44.038
Golden rule.

74
00:02:44.318 --> 00:02:46.921
Answer only what's asked, honestly, briefly.

75
00:02:47.201 --> 00:02:52.875
Keep documents ready: passport, visa, return ticket, hotel booking, invitation letter.

76
00:02:54.225 --> 00:02:55.569
Here is a quick table:

77
00:02:55.849 --> 00:02:57.791
Officer asks, and Good answer.

78
00:02:58.071 --> 00:02:59.607
What's the purpose of your visit?:

79
00:02:59.887 --> 00:03:00.697
Business.

80
00:03:00.977 --> 00:03:03.751
I'm attending a tech conference. / Tourism.

81
00:03:04.031 --> 00:03:05.396
How long will you stay?:

82
00:03:05.676 --> 00:03:06.700
Five days.

83
00:03:06.980 --> 00:03:08.452
I return on the 12th.

84
00:03:08.732 --> 00:03:09.969
Where will you be staying?:

85
00:03:10.249 --> 00:03:12.468
At the Marina Hotel, here's the booking.

86
00:03:12.748 --> 00:03:14.881
Who is your employer or what do you do?:

87
00:03:15.161 --> 00:03:18.639
I'm a senior software engineer at XYZ Technologies.

88
00:03:18.919 --> 00:03:20.391
Have you been here before?:

89
00:03:20.671 --> 00:03:24.575
Yes, once in 2024. / No, first time.

90
00:03:24.855 --> 00:03:26.881
Are you carrying more than X in cash?:

91
00:03:27.161 --> 00:03:29.743
No. / Yes, here's my declaration.

92
00:03:30.023 --> 00:03:31.601
Do you have a return ticket?:

93
00:03:31.881 --> 00:03:33.033
Yes, here it is.

94
00:03:34.383 --> 00:03:35.685
If you don't understand:

95
00:03:35.965 --> 00:03:37.842
Sorry, could you repeat that, please?

96
00:03:38.122 --> 00:03:38.997
Don't guess.

97
00:03:40.347 --> 00:03:41.264
Part 4.

98
00:03:41.544 --> 00:03:42.952
At the gate and boarding.

99
00:03:44.202 --> 00:03:45.183
You can ask:

100
00:03:45.463 --> 00:03:48.194
Excuse me, is this the gate for the Mumbai flight?

101
00:03:48.474 --> 00:03:51.055
Has boarding started for AI 302?

102
00:03:51.335 --> 00:03:52.615
Is the flight delayed?

103
00:03:52.895 --> 00:03:54.197
Do you know the new time?

104
00:03:54.477 --> 00:03:56.055
Which boarding group am I in?

105
00:03:56.335 --> 00:03:59.877
Can I take this bag on board, or does it need to be gate-checked?

106
00:04:00.157 --> 00:04:01.543
Announcements decoded:

107
00:04:02.893 --> 00:04:04.237
Here is a quick table:

108
00:04:04.517 --> 00:04:05.861
Announcement, and Meaning.

109
00:04:06.141 --> 00:04:09.704
Pre-boarding for families and passengers needing assistance:

110
00:04:09.984 --> 00:04:11.883
Not you yet (unless it applies).

111
00:04:12.163 --> 00:04:13.869
Now boarding zones 1 and 2:

112
00:04:14.149 --> 00:04:16.133
Check your boarding pass zone or group.

113
00:04:16.413 --> 00:04:18.184
Final call for passenger...:

114
00:04:18.464 --> 00:04:19.189
Hurry!

115
00:04:19.469 --> 00:04:20.728
The gate is closing.

116
00:04:21.008 --> 00:04:22.032
Gate change:

117
00:04:22.312 --> 00:04:24.509
Check the screens, move to the new gate.

118
00:04:25.859 --> 00:04:26.819
Part 5.

119
00:04:27.099 --> 00:04:28.017
On the plane.

120
00:04:29.267 --> 00:04:31.293
Excuse me, I think you're in my seat.

121
00:04:31.573 --> 00:04:32.725
I'm 14C.

122
00:04:33.005 --> 00:04:34.605
(show boarding pass, smile).

123
00:04:34.885 --> 00:04:37.296
Could you help me put my bag in the overhead bin?

124
00:04:37.576 --> 00:04:39.411
Could I have a glass of water, please?

125
00:04:39.691 --> 00:04:41.397
Is it possible to change seats?

126
00:04:41.677 --> 00:04:43.256
There's an empty one at the back.

127
00:04:43.536 --> 00:04:45.264
Excuse me, could I get past?

128
00:04:45.544 --> 00:04:46.376
Thank you.

129
00:04:46.656 --> 00:04:48.789
What time do we land (local time)?

130
00:04:50.139 --> 00:04:51.078
Part 6.

131
00:04:51.358 --> 00:04:52.211
Arrival.

132
00:04:53.461 --> 00:04:54.293
Baggage.

133
00:04:54.573 --> 00:04:58.157
Which belt is the bag from flight SQ 421 on?

134
00:04:58.437 --> 00:05:01.467
Where is the baggage services or lost and found desk?

135
00:05:02.817 --> 00:05:04.395
Lost or damaged bag.

136
00:05:04.675 --> 00:05:05.614
You could say:

137
00:05:05.894 --> 00:05:10.651
Hi, my bag didn't arrive on flight SQ 421 from Bangalore.

138
00:05:10.931 --> 00:05:12.382
Here's my baggage tag.

139
00:05:12.662 --> 00:05:15.243
It's a large black suitcase with a red ribbon.

140
00:05:15.523 --> 00:05:16.889
Could you file a report?

141
00:05:17.169 --> 00:05:20.518
When can I expect it, and can it be delivered to my hotel?

142
00:05:20.798 --> 00:05:23.123
Is there an allowance for essentials meanwhile?

143
00:05:24.473 --> 00:05:29.103
Always get a reference number (PIR) and a phone or email for follow-up.

144
00:05:30.453 --> 00:05:31.306
Customs.

145
00:05:31.586 --> 00:05:32.930
Here is a quick table:

146
00:05:33.210 --> 00:05:34.426
Asked, and Answer.

147
00:05:34.706 --> 00:05:35.965
Anything to declare?:

148
00:05:36.245 --> 00:05:38.591
No, nothing. / Yes, I have item.

149
00:05:38.871 --> 00:05:40.450
Are you carrying food items?:

150
00:05:40.730 --> 00:05:41.605
Be honest:

151
00:05:41.885 --> 00:05:43.421
Yes, some packaged snacks.

152
00:05:44.771 --> 00:05:45.645
Part 8.

153
00:05:45.925 --> 00:05:47.099
When things go wrong.

154
00:05:48.349 --> 00:05:49.927
Flight delayed or cancelled.

155
00:05:50.207 --> 00:05:51.146
You could say:

156
00:05:51.426 --> 00:05:53.495
My flight to Delhi has been cancelled.

157
00:05:53.775 --> 00:05:55.013
What are my options?

158
00:05:55.293 --> 00:05:57.789
Can you rebook me on the next available flight?

159
00:05:58.069 --> 00:06:00.906
Will the airline provide a hotel or meal voucher?

160
00:06:01.186 --> 00:06:02.765
And can I get that in writing?

161
00:06:04.115 --> 00:06:05.203
Missed connection.

162
00:06:05.483 --> 00:06:06.421
You could say:

163
00:06:06.701 --> 00:06:10.349
My first flight was delayed and I missed my connection to London.

164
00:06:10.629 --> 00:06:12.037
Here's my boarding pass.

165
00:06:12.317 --> 00:06:13.896
Can you put me on the next flight?

166
00:06:14.176 --> 00:06:16.267
Will my checked bag be transferred too?

167
00:06:17.617 --> 00:06:19.259
Can't find your gate or lost.

168
00:06:19.539 --> 00:06:20.478
You could say:

169
00:06:20.758 --> 00:06:22.529
Excuse me, I'm a bit lost.

170
00:06:22.809 --> 00:06:26.307
How do I get to the international transfers or Gate B12?

171
00:06:26.587 --> 00:06:28.998
Is it a long walk, or should I take the train?

172
00:06:30.348 --> 00:06:31.244
Part 9.

173
00:06:31.524 --> 00:06:32.591
Vocabulary.

174
00:06:33.841 --> 00:06:35.185
Here is a quick table:

175
00:06:35.465 --> 00:06:36.595
Word, and Meaning.

176
00:06:36.875 --> 00:06:38.326
Layover or Stopover:

177
00:06:38.606 --> 00:06:40.782
A stop between flights (short or long).

178
00:06:41.062 --> 00:06:42.470
Transit or Transfer:

179
00:06:42.750 --> 00:06:43.859
Changing planes.

180
00:06:44.139 --> 00:06:45.121
Boarding pass:

181
00:06:45.401 --> 00:06:46.979
The pass that lets you board.

182
00:06:47.259 --> 00:06:48.689
Carry-on or Cabin bag:

183
00:06:48.969 --> 00:06:50.398
Bag you take on the plane.

184
00:06:50.678 --> 00:06:51.766
Checked baggage:

185
00:06:52.046 --> 00:06:53.518
Bag that goes in the hold.

186
00:06:53.798 --> 00:06:54.950
Excess baggage:

187
00:06:55.230 --> 00:06:56.873
Weight over the allowance (fee).

188
00:06:57.153 --> 00:06:58.731
Departures or Arrivals:

189
00:06:59.011 --> 00:07:00.569
Leaving or coming areas.

190
00:07:00.849 --> 00:07:01.830
Duty-free:

191
00:07:02.110 --> 00:07:04.009
Tax-free shops after security.

192
00:07:05.359 --> 00:07:06.276
Jet lag:

193
00:07:06.556 --> 00:07:08.369
Tiredness from time-zone change.

194
00:07:08.649 --> 00:07:09.460
Red-eye:

195
00:07:09.740 --> 00:07:10.871
Overnight flight.

196
00:07:12.221 --> 00:07:13.074
Part 10.

197
00:07:13.354 --> 00:07:14.783
Practice conversations.

198
00:07:16.033 --> 00:07:17.633
Check-in with extra baggage.

199
00:07:17.913 --> 00:07:19.940
Here is how the conversation goes.

200
00:07:20.220 --> 00:07:21.628
Good morning.

201
00:07:21.908 --> 00:07:23.657
Passport and ticket, please.

202
00:07:23.937 --> 00:07:25.025
Good morning.

203
00:07:25.305 --> 00:07:26.457
Here you are.

204
00:07:26.737 --> 00:07:28.423
I'm flying to Dubai.

205
00:07:28.703 --> 00:07:30.473
How many bags are you checking in?

206
00:07:30.753 --> 00:07:31.777
Two bags.

207
00:07:32.057 --> 00:07:33.913
Your allowance is 30 kilos.

208
00:07:34.193 --> 00:07:36.177
Together they're 34 kilos.

209
00:07:37.527 --> 00:07:39.127
The conversation continues.

210
00:07:39.407 --> 00:07:40.133
Oh.

211
00:07:40.413 --> 00:07:43.079
Can I move some things to my cabin bag?

212
00:07:43.359 --> 00:07:45.237
Sure, you can use the side area.

213
00:07:45.517 --> 00:07:46.711
Five minutes later

214
00:07:46.991 --> 00:07:48.613
I've moved some clothes.

215
00:07:48.893 --> 00:07:50.535
Could you weigh them again?

216
00:07:50.815 --> 00:07:52.821
29.5 kilos.

217
00:07:53.101 --> 00:07:54.146
Perfect.

218
00:07:54.426 --> 00:07:55.834
Window or aisle?

219
00:07:57.184 --> 00:07:58.784
The conversation continues.

220
00:07:59.064 --> 00:08:00.323
Aisle, please.

221
00:08:00.603 --> 00:08:03.312
And could you add my frequent flyer number?

222
00:08:03.592 --> 00:08:04.424
Done.

223
00:08:04.704 --> 00:08:07.371
Boarding is at 9:10 from gate 24.

224
00:08:07.651 --> 00:08:08.568
Thank you!

225
00:08:09.918 --> 00:08:11.305
Flight delay at the gate.

226
00:08:11.585 --> 00:08:13.611
Here is how the conversation goes.

227
00:08:13.891 --> 00:08:17.347
Excuse me, the board says the Delhi flight is delayed.

228
00:08:17.627 --> 00:08:19.099
Do you know the new time?

229
00:08:19.379 --> 00:08:22.515
Yes, it's now 4:30 instead of 2:45.

230
00:08:22.795 --> 00:08:24.353
There's a technical issue.

231
00:08:24.633 --> 00:08:27.470
I have a connecting flight in Delhi at 7.

232
00:08:27.750 --> 00:08:29.030
Will I make it?

233
00:08:29.310 --> 00:08:30.462
It will be tight.

234
00:08:30.742 --> 00:08:33.942
Let me check if we can protect you on the 9 pm connection.

235
00:08:35.292 --> 00:08:36.892
The conversation continues.

236
00:08:37.172 --> 00:08:38.111
Thank you.

237
00:08:38.391 --> 00:08:40.524
Will my bag also be moved?

238
00:08:40.804 --> 00:08:42.169
Yes, it's checked through.

239
00:08:42.449 --> 00:08:44.391
Here's a meal voucher for the delay.

240
00:08:44.671 --> 00:08:45.481
Thanks.

241
00:08:45.761 --> 00:08:49.217
Could you write the new connection details on my boarding pass?

242
00:08:50.567 --> 00:08:52.103
That's the end of this lesson.

243
00:08:52.383 --> 00:08:57.034
Pick one script from it, say it out loud three times, and use it for real today.

244
00:08:57.314 --> 00:09:03.437
For extra practice, paste the Master Prompt into an AI assistant and role-play the conversation.

